     48 h budget, window 19 to 21 UTC (after dark) lid 4S12.40P, +107.2 Wh usable
     48 h budget, any time (converter on 24 h)     lid 4S13.42P, +139.7 Wh usable
     72 h no tablet budget                         lid 4S11.16P, +68.1 Wh usable
     72 h budget, window 13 to 15 UTC              lid 4S11.79P, +88.0 Wh usable
     72 h budget, window 10 to 12 UTC              lid 4S11.79P, +88.0 Wh usable
     72 h budget, window 19 to 21 UTC (after dark) lid 4S13.15P, +130.9 Wh usable
     72 h budget, any time (converter on 24 h)     lid 4S15.25P, +197.4 Wh usable
   Why the daylight windows read alike, from the model's own trace (NOM, TYP, 72 h, the lid at 4S11.79P, the 06 UTC
   start's second day, window W13):
     node power at 08/09/10/11/12/13/14/15/16/17 UTC: 104 121 121 121 121 121 121 102 60 16 W
     level at 121.4 W (the path's limit in the model) from 09 to 14 UTC; both windows' hours inside it: yes
     the store's highest that day: base 212.5 of 218.4 Wh, lid 358.3 of 372.2 Wh: never full
   So every Wh the tablet takes in a daylight window is a Wh the packs do not take, whichever level hours the window
   holds. After dark it comes from the store directly; with the converter enabled all day the idle draw of section 1
   is added for 24 h

